    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "doc: \"How to Upgrade\" release notes section is outdated since the `bitcoin` wrapper executable",
    "body": "The \"How to Upgrade\" [section](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/doc/release-notes-empty-template.md#how-to-upgrade) of the release notes template suggests:\n\n> ... just copy over ... `bitcoind`/`bitcoin-qt` (on Linux).\n\nThis seems outdated since https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/31375, which introduced the `bitcoin` wrapper executable. Copying only `bitcoind`/`bitcoin-qt` would leave the `bitcoin` wrapper (and the multiprocess binaries in `libexec/`) at the old version.",
